1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,895
Module 11 starts with schedules — running an agent or workflow unattended.

2
00:00:03,895 --> 00:00:07,000
The guardrails come first, before the first run, not after.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,958
Go to Automation, Schedules, New schedule.

4
00:00:08,958 --> 00:00:18,000
You pick what to run — an agent or a workflow — how often, either an interval preset or a cron expression, and where the results land: a new chat, appended to an existing one, or a notification.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,558
Before the first scheduled run: set a spend cap in Settings, Usage.

6
00:00:21,558 --> 00:00:30,000
This is a hard prerequisite, not a nice-to-have — an unattended job with no cap can run far longer, and cost far more, than anyone would approve in the moment.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,681
Also turn on “keep running in the tray” in Settings, General, so schedules fire even when the window's closed.

8
00:00:35,681 --> 00:00:39,967
One catch: a missed run — say the machine was asleep — does not fire retroactively.

9
00:00:39,967 --> 00:00:41,000
It's simply skipped.

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,719
The worked example: a morning briefing.

11
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:46,508
An agent runs daily, checks a few sources, and posts a short digest as a notification.

12
00:00:46,508 --> 00:00:54,000
The instruction that keeps it worth opening after two weeks: “if nothing needs my attention, say so plainly” — so a quiet day produces one honest line instead of padding.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,441
The gotcha: good schedule candidates report — they draft, summarize, and tell you.

14
00:00:57,441 --> 00:01:02,392
Poor candidates act unreviewed — sending mail, posting publicly, committing code — with nobody watching in the moment.

15
00:01:02,392 --> 00:01:06,000
Draft-and-tell beats do-it-automatically for anything that isn't trivially reversible.

16
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,429
Presets don't cover every cadence.

17
00:01:07,429 --> 00:01:11,000
Next, a quick reference for cron expressions when the schedule you need is irregular.

